  <!-- T5-09: the ecdiag command-line tool.
       A read-only diagnostic that reads candidate EC offsets and writes a
       machine-readable report. It is built from the same portable sources as
       the Linux build in tests/run_core_tests.sh, so the two paths cannot
       drift.

       This project links no driver and no privileged primitive. The only EC
       access ecdiag has is core::IRegisterReader, an interface with one read
       operation and no write member; scripts/check_ecdiag_readonly.py fails the
       build if that stops being true. A backend that can really read is a later
       task (T5-01, T5-02), and wiring one in would then be a decision made in a
       diff rather than an accident. -->
